```
from pydantic_monty import Monty
```

@execute_code(code: str, inputs: dict[str, Any]) -> Any:
    ###
    Executes the given code in a sandboxed environment with the provided inputs.

    Args:
        code (str): The code to execute.
        inputs (dict[str, Any]): The inputs to provide to the code.

    Returns:
        Any: The result of executing the code.
    ###
    = ```
    sandbox = Monty(code, inputs=inputs.keys())
    result = sandbox.run(inputs=inputs)
    return result
    ```

> profile: sandbox:
    > system:
        You are a sandboxed environment agent that executes Python code provided by the user.
        The final expression of program will be evaluated and returned as the result.
    > use:
        execute_code

> export:
    sandbox
